\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
% TRANSFORMATION TPosDeletion
< m1: SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}
              [ I1:mu1,
                posrel/POS(KEY_POSkey){POSrec1},
                I2:mu2,
                predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}[mu3],
                mu4
              ]
>

< m : SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}
              [ I1:mu1,
                I2:mu2,
                predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}[mu3],
                mu4
              ]
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: ALL (mu1, I11:rel1/..)
       I2: ALL (mu2, I21:rel2/..)
         I11: QUOTE_SRelPrec(rel1, posrel) AND
              NOT rel1 IN [negrel, meltnegrel, posrel]
         I21: QUOTE_SRelPrec(posrel, rel2) AND
              NOT rel2 IN [negrel, meltnegrel, posrel]
       m : EXIST (mu1, [I31:auxrel/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu5]]) AND
           ( SENTENCErec1.mood = declarative OR
             ( SENTENCErec1.mood = whinterrogative AND
               NOT EXIST (mu1, [subjrel/..]) )
           )
         I31: VERBrec1.subc = doaux
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1: @
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1: @
         >
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TPosDeletion
\item[* relevant examples:] \mbox{}\\
1. He did POS go to church $\leftrightarrow$ He did go to church\\
2. Who did POS give you the chocolate $\leftrightarrow$ Who did give you the 
chocolate
3. He has POS gone to church $\rightarrow$ He has gone to church (in generation 
only)\\
4. POS to go to church $\rightarrow$ To go to church (in generation only)\\
5. Whom did you POS see leave $\rightarrow$ Whom did you see leave (in 
generation only)\\
6. Did he POS go to school $\rightarrow$ Did he go to school (in generation 
only)
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] CLAUSEtoSENTENCE
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) TC\_Dodeletion
\item[* date of creation:] 9-JUN-1988 15:04:56  
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:]
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To delete POS whenever it occurs. In analysis, POS is introduced 
only for those cases where there is a `do' which cannot be explained otherwise, 
i.e.\ the English sentence {\em 
He can come\/} will never get a POS, and hence will not translate into Dutch 
{\em Hij kan wel komen\/}. (If necessary, a rule can be added in future that 
does introduce POS here in case the auxiliary is written with an accent or in 
italics/underlined: He {\em can\/} come, He c\`{a}n come, He \underline{can} 
come)
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:] see above under `task'
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[\ \ consequences in the grammar:]
\item[\ \ translation aspects:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate} 
\item within this language:\\

\item in other languages:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[* relevant literature/documents:]
\item[\ \ remarks:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item problems:\\
A false path is created in analysis for those cases where the negrel has 
`integrated' with the operator to form one complex verb ({\em didn't\/}): {\em 
He didn't see it\/} has no negrel and has an auxrel with verb.subc = doaux, and 
will hence introduce a POS here. The solution is to give such an integrated 
verb a new subc, e.g.\ {\em donotaux\/}.
\item modifications:\\

\end{enumerate}
\end{description}

\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
% TRANSFORMATION TNoDeletion1
< m1: SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}
              [ I1:mu1,
                I4:sig1,
                I2:mu2,
                predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                       [ I3:mu3,
                         I6:sig2,
                         I5:mu5
                       ],
                mu6
              ]
>

< m: SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}
              [ I1:mu1,
                I4:sig1,
                I2:mu2,
                predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                       [ I3:mu3,
                         I6:sig2,
                         I5:mu5
                       ],
                mu6
              ]
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: ALL (mu1, I11:rel1/..) AND 
           NOT EXIST (mu1, [auxrel/..]) 
       I2: ALL (mu2, I21:rel2/..) AND
           NOT EXIST (mu2, [auxrel/..])
         I11: QUOTE_SRelPrec(rel1, auxrel)
         I21: QUOTE_SRelPrec(auxrel, rel2) 
       I3: NOT EXIST (mu3, [head/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu4]])
       I4: ALL (sig1, auxrel/..)
       I5: NOT EXIST (mu5, [head/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu4]])
       I6: ALL (sig2, head/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu4])
       m1: NOT EXIST (mu2, [posrel/..]) AND
           ( NOT EXIST (sig1, [auxrel/I31::VERB{VERBrec2}[mu7]]) OR
             NOT EXIST (sig2, [head/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu4]]) OR
             NOT ALL (mu2, I32:rel3/..) OR
             NOT ALL (mu3, I33:rel4/..) )
       m : ( SENTENCErec1.finiteness = infinite OR
             EXIST (sig1, [auxrel/..]) OR
             EXIST (sig2, [head/I22::VERB{VERBrec3}[mu8]]) OR
             EXIST (mu1, [conjrel/..]) )
           AND
           ( NOT EXIST (sig1, [auxrel/I31::VERB{VERBrec2}[mu7]]) OR
             NOT EXIST (sig2, [head/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu4]]) OR
             NOT ALL (mu2, I32:rel3/..) OR
             NOT ALL (mu3, I33:rel4/..) )
         I22: VERBrec3.subc = beverb
         I31: VERBrec2.subc = doaux
         I32: rel3 IN AUX_postAuxAdvRels
         I33: rel4 IN AUX_beginVPAdvRels
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1: @
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1: @
         >
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TNoDeletion1
\item[* relevant examples:] He has never seen me, (I like) swimming, Didn't 
you know? Has he a book?
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] CLAUSEtoSENTENCE
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) TC\_DoDeletion
\item[* date of creation:] 9-JUN-1988 15:53:01  
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:]
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] to let sentences in which nothing is to be deleted pass this 
transformation class. 
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals) The real 
conditions, which are not symmetric between generation and analysis, are given 
in the matchconditions on the entire models:\\
1. Generation: do not accept sentences with a posrel (they go to TPosDeletion), 
and do not accept sentences which have an auxrel/do that is separated from the 
head/verb only by an adverbial (these should have the `do' deleted, which is 
done in TDoDeletion).\\
2. Analysis: Do not accept sentences which have an auxrel/do that is separated 
from the head/verb only by an adverbial (these must have a POS inserted, which 
is done in TPosDeletion), and do not accept finite sentences which have no 
conjrel or auxrel at all (they must receive the operator `do', which is done by 
TDoDeletion).\\
Asymmetry between analysis and generation is caused by POS: in analysis,
a POS is never introduced unless there is good reason for it.
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:] see above under `strategy'
